<title>UK: Howard Davies confirmed as head of Britain's SIB.</title>
<headline>Howard Davies confirmed as head of Britain's SIB.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chancellor of the Exchequer Gordon Brown on Thursday formally announced the appointment of Howard Davies as chairman of Britain's revamped Securities and Investments Board.</p>
<p>Davies, who has been deputy governor at the Bank of England since late-1995, will serve a five-year term from August 1.</p>
<p>Lord Runciman has been reappointed as a Deputy Chairman for a further year from the same date.</p>
<p>Davies will be responsible for carrying forward the establishment of a single regulatory body to oversee all the financial markets.</p>
<p>David Clementi, just appointed as Deputy Governor of the Bank of England, has also been appointed a Director of the Securities and Investments Board.</p>
<p>-- Mike Peacock, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
